[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The purpose of this document is to outline the design specifications of the GBSK Main Control Application Firmware.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document describes the design modules and sub-modules of the GBSK Main Control Application Firmware.

The information in this document is derived from the Main Control Application FW SRS, referenced in this document.

\*The term Software applies to both Software and Firmware components.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
FW
  Firmware

MCU
  Microcontroller Unit

PRS
  Product Requirements Specification

SDP
  Software Development Plan

SRS
  Software Requirements Specification

SW
  Software
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control application firmware serves as the main logical control for system operation.

The main control application firmware monitors all the inputs from the various connections on the board hardware. It can also be used to set and control many of the components that the main control board interfaces with. For off the shelf components, the main control application can set/enable the Peltier cooler temperature, can set/enable the motor controller drivers for cooling system pump and fans, and can enable the ion pump controller.
<<<

