[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-178
TITLE: External DAC communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware communicates with two external DAC IC chips. It communicates with both chips on a singular SPI bus, but with independent chip select and load signals for each chip. The external DAC module waits for any queued-up requests by the rest of the firmware to write new DAC values. In case multiple DAC values are queued up simultaneous or in quick succession, the DAC module processes them in FIFO (first in first out) fashion, waiting for the SPI bus to be free until the next value is processed.

The DAC module utilizes the manufacturer's hardware abstraction library to write serial data to the SPI bus. The writes to the SPI bus are non-block interrupt-based calls which allows the processor to continue operating during the relatively longer SPI transmission (compared to processing speed). The DAC module utilizes the SPI interrupt handler to set flags for handling the queued DAC requests (indicating bus is free).

In addition to sending data over the SPI bus, the DAC module handles the digital chip select and load signals. These signals are independent for each chip, so there are a total of 4 digital output lines controlled by the DAC via the hardware abstraction library's provided GPIO control.

Each DAC IC controls four separate channels, although on the board only three channels on each DAC IC are utilized. One DAC IC sets the analog voltage for the heatsink fan control, cabinet fan control, and coolant pump motor control. The second DAC IC sets the analog voltage for the X-coil deflection control, Y-coil deflection control, and focus coil control.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-55
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
