  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-179
TITLE: Backup Timer Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware communicates with two external backup timers. It communicates with both timers on a singular I2C bus, with the main microcontroller acting as master to the two slave timers. The timer module alternates between each timer, continuously communicating with the two timers. As the two timers are slave devices, they require the master to initiate communication. The main microcontroller will send commands to the timers which include read time, set timer period, pause counting, and clear timer period. The timers will always report back their timer counter value in response to each command. The 'read time' command is simply for the timer to do nothing other than report the time back.

The I2C communication with the timers is performed using the manufacturer provided 'HRI' library or hardware register interface. This HRI library is used to set up interrupt-based communication on the I2C bus instead of having blocking commands wait for completion of writes and reads of the I2C bus which are relatively long in duration compared to the processing speed of the main microcontroller unit.

In case anyone external IC does not respond, the I2C bus is monitored for any NACK values indicating a non-response. The firmware will report a fault if no response is detected from one of the ADC ICs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-11
  ROLE: Refines
