[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-180
TITLE: Bootloading and Debug Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware communicates with the PC via one of the microcontrollers' serial UART interface. The firmware both receives and transmits data on this UART port. Due to the nature of UART having independent transmit and receive lines, the transmit and receive functionality operate independently. As the UART baud rate is relatively slow compared to the processing speed of the microcontroller, both sending and receiving data is performed with non-blocking interrupt callback functions.

Transmitted data is sent as a buffer of bytes, representing a singular data packet to the PC, with the interrupt callback occurring once all data bytes have been transmitted. The firmware sets a flag when transmission is initiated, and clears the flag after transmission is finished, to not create transmission conflicts on the transmit line.

Reception is performed one byte at a time, with the interrupt callback occurring once a data byte is available. The parsing of the received byte is done to determine whether a complete data packet has been received from the PC, as according to the communication protocol. Once a completed data packet has been received, the firmware sets a flag for further data processing outside of the parsing inside of the interrupt callback.

The firmware will monitor for a boot load command from the PC. Once received the firmware will reset the microcontroller into bootloader mode.
<<<
