[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-188
TITLE: General System Monitoring: Fan Control
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware periodically evaluates temperature feedback and the current system state to
control cooling outputs. While high voltage can be present from setup through discharge,
the cabinet fan is driven at 4.9 V. Otherwise the cabinet fan uses nominal 30°C, 25°C, and
20°C transition points for 4.9 V, 4.5 V, and 4.1 V operation, with a 3.7 V minimum and
2°C downward hysteresis.

Enabling the coolant pump cancels a pending shutdown, asserts the pump output, and drives
its fan at 1.85 V. A request to disable an active pump keeps the pump and fan operating for
three minutes of post-operation cooling; expiry then deasserts the pump and sets its fan
voltage to zero.

The heatsink fan is adjusted based on heatsink-temperature feedback, with higher
temperatures corresponding to higher fan speeds.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-63
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-65
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-189
TITLE: General System Monitoring: System Faults
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware periodically evaluates measured and reported feedback to detect cooling
faults. Coolant temperature above 35°C, Peltier heatsink temperature above 50°C, and
cabinet temperature above 40°C produce their corresponding temperature fault reports.
Coolant pressure and flow limits are evaluated while the pump is operating; pressure
debounce counters are cleared while it is off so stale samples cannot cause a later fault.

The same monitoring cycle also detects communication timeouts, interlock faults, ion
repeller overcurrent or voltage deviations, and deflection or focus-coil feedback
deviations.
<<<
