[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-190
TITLE: State: Startup
STATEMENT: >>>
The startup state is the initial state of the firmware after device reset. No faults are processed during this state, the system can only exit fault state into cold once an 'initialize' command is received from the PC. The purpose of this state is to allow the PC and other parts of the system, which may have longer power on times, initialize before regular system operation commences.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-38
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-39
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-191
TITLE: State: Cold
STATEMENT: >>>
The cold state is for when the system has been initialized, but the filament and high voltage are off. Any faults which occur transition the system into cold fault mode. From cold state, the system can transition to the conditioning state if the PC sends a conditioning command. The firmware can also transition into the warmup state if the PC sends a warmup command.
<<<
