  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-192
TITLE: State: Cold Fault
STATEMENT: >>>
The cold fault state is for when a system error has occurred, but the system does not have the filament running. The firmware can transition out of the cold fault state and into the cold state after receiving a reset fault command from the PC.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-33
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-193
TITLE: State: Conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
On entry to conditioning, the firmware sets the requested filament current, enables the
coolant pump, and clears the conditioning hold timer. The first indication that the HVPS
filament has reached and stabilized at the target starts a 9,000-deci-second (15-minute)
hold. Later stabilization indications do not restart an active hold. When the timer expires,
the firmware marks it completed before queuing one completion event and transitions to
primed state.

A PC stop returns the system to cold state. A fault during conditioning transitions the
system to warmup-fault state.
<<<
