  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-37
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-194
TITLE: State: Warmup
STATEMENT: >>>
The warmup state is for when the system is ramping up the filament current to reach a level where the filament is at a temperature that can sustain lower levels of emission. Due to the nature of the HVPS filament control (constant current) and the system characteristics (increased resistance with increased temperature), and the nature of the filament and cathode sensitivity, it is not advisable to go to a higher current which could sustain the intended target levels of emission output.

Before queuing entry to warmup, the PC command handler requires COLD state, verifies both
emergency-stop inputs, and then validates the target. An open emergency stop produces an
``SPR_ACCESS_ERROR`` response rather than acknowledging a transition that cannot occur.
The state-entry handler verifies the emergency stops again; failure reports an interlock
fault and returns before changing the heater, coolant pump, or state.

Warmup completes once the reported filament value from the HVPS interface board stabilizes at the target filament current. The firmware will transition to primed state once that target setpoint has been reached if no current plan is loaded, otherwise it will transition to the staged state.

If the PC sends a stop command in the warmup state, the firmware will transition back to the cold state. If a fault occurs during the warmup state, the system will instead transition to the warmup fault state.
<<<
