- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-41
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-76
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-195
TITLE: State: Warmup Fault
STATEMENT: >>>
The warmup fault state is for when a system error has occurred when warming up the filament such as during the conditioning state or the warmup state. The firmware can transition out of the warmup fault state and into the cold state after receiving a reset fault command from the PC.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-13
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-22
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-196
TITLE: State: Primed
STATEMENT: >>>
The primed state is for when the filament of the system is at the warmup value, but no plan is loaded, nor has any plan loading been initiated. On an error, the system enters fault state. On a standby event, which can be initiated by the PC or after a timeout, the firmware transitions from primed state to discharge state. If the firmware receives a new session command in primed, it will begin a new session and transition the state into the staging state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-42
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-197
TITLE: State: Staging
STATEMENT: >>>
The staging state is for when the PC is actively loading the parameters for a new treatment plan. On an error, the system enters fault state. On a standby event, which can be initiated by the PC or after a timeout, the firmware transitions from the staging state to discharge state. If the firmware receives a wipe plan command, it will transition the state back to primed. If the PC sends a command to finalize the staging of the plan, the firmware will transition the state from staging to staged.
<<<
