[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-198
TITLE: State: Staged
STATEMENT: >>>
The staged state is for when the PC has completed loading one scalar emission but has not
yet released it for execution. Before plan release is allowed, the PC must confirm that
emission.

On an error, the system enters fault state. On standby, the firmware transitions to
discharge. A wipe command returns it to primed. A valid plan release after scalar
confirmation transitions the system into the HVPS check state.
<<<
