  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-201
TITLE: State: Ready
STATEMENT: >>>
The ready state is for when the system has high voltage ramped to the scalar emission
setpoint but has not begun emission. On an error the firmware transitions to fault. A stop
command transitions to termination, and a standby command or timeout transitions to
discharge. Only an explicit point-scope release command from the PC transitions to
launching; there is no automatic release path.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-17
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-18
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-202
TITLE: State: Launching
STATEMENT: >>>
The launching state ramps filament current and sets the deflection and focusing coil outputs while
emission remains disabled. For an ordinary emission, reaching the HVPS setpoint permits the
transition to Emission. For a QC-armed emission, the firmware first sends the head-interface
Accumulating command and remains in Launching until the head reports an Active edge. A stale
Complete report cannot satisfy this gate. Head command retries are bounded; a timeout or Error
keeps radiation disabled, sends a Stopped command, reports a QC fault, and transitions through the
normal fault handling. A PC Clear Faults command resets the main QC session and its PC result to
Idle/zero, retransmits Stopped until the head confirms a safe terminal state, and accepts the
head's retained Error state as confirmation that acquisition is no longer active. A PC stop
transitions to Termination.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-16
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-70
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-203
TITLE: State: Emission
STATEMENT: >>>
The emission state is when the system is performing radiation emission output. On an
error, the system enters fault state. If the PC sends a stop command, the firmware
transitions to termination so the same remaining time can be reconfirmed and resumed.

When the scalar emission completes without interruption, the firmware always transitions
to discharge. It never returns to setup for another point in the same session.
<<<
