[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-204
TITLE: State: Termination
STATEMENT: >>>
The termination state is for the system to ramp down high voltage and turn off the coil outputs after the termination of a treatment plan or operational point. The termination state, however, maintains the filament current value at the targeted warmup setpoint. On an error, the system enters fault state. Otherwise, once termination of the high voltage is completed, the firmware transitions to the staged state. The firmware transitions to this state as a plan still loaded, even if the loaded treatment plan has already been fully completed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-80
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-85
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-205
TITLE: State: Discharge
STATEMENT: >>>
The discharge state is for the system to turn off both the high voltage and the filament current. On an error, the system enters fault state. On completion of the discharge, the firmware transitions to cold state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-80
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-86
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-206
TITLE: States: Fault Discharge and Fault
STATEMENT: >>>
When a fault is detected from an operating state in which high voltage or filament power
may still be energized, the firmware enters Fault Discharge. Entry disables the
high-voltage interlock, pauses the external timers, disables the emission indicators,
commands the HVPS kV, filament, and grid setpoints to zero, and commands all three coil
outputs to zero. The cabinet fan remains at high speed during this discharge.

Fault Discharge continues until kV feedback is below 4 kV, filament feedback is at or
below 700 mA, and the HVPS warming status is clear. The firmware then enters the latched
Fault state, disables the emission and grid interlocks, and reasserts the zero output
commands. A further fault event during Fault Discharge transitions immediately to Fault.
<<<
