[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-207
TITLE: System Status (Telemetry)
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware collects monitored values in a system-status array used as the source of truth
for firmware decisions and telemetry serialization. Every 10 ms, it serializes the array
and sends it to the CNC. The telemetry layout appends the raw state-dependent
required-interlock mask and publishes the complete physical and required interlock masks,
head-interface coolant values, buttons, collimator ID, and magnetometer values. Telemetry
requests use the same serializer.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-83
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-208
TITLE: Treatment Session (Scalar Emission)
STATEMENT: >>>
Each treatment session stores exactly one scalar operational point. The point contains
total treatment time, remaining treatment time, high-voltage kV, target emission current
mA, filament current, and X, Y, and focus coil currents. The session contains no point
count, point index, or automatic-execution field.
<<<
